{"parentUuid":"f7b0e1b0-2ad6-4e72-9db2-68a830f8ff92","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a43c2688668dbd6d4","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdkPjsknMXwtCAVSt7yBk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything needed. This is the **memos** project (Go). Here are my findings.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis repository implements third-party identity provider authentication (SSO / federated login) under `internal/idp`. The design is a small provider abstraction plus a single concrete protocol implementation (OAuth2).\n\n### 1. Provider abstraction package\n\n**Package path:** `internal/idp` (import: `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/idp`)\n**File:** `/bench/repo/internal/idp/idp.go`\n\nThis package defines the shared identity-provider concept. It is intentionally minimal — an 8-line file declaring the normalized user-info struct that every provider implementation must return:\n\n```go\npackage idp\n\ntype IdentityProviderUserInfo struct {\n\tIdentifier  string\n\tDisplayName string\n\tEmail       string\n\tAvatarURL   string\n}\n```\n\nNote: the abstraction here is a shared data contract (`IdentityProviderUserInfo`) rather than a Go `interface`. The concrete package imports `internal/idp` and returns this type from its `UserInfo` method, so `internal/idp` is the abstraction/parent package that ties provider implementations together.\n\n### 2. Concrete protocol implementation package\n\n**Package path:** `internal/idp/oauth2` (import: `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/idp/oauth2`)\n**Files:** `/bench/repo/internal/idp/oauth2/oauth2.go` (impl), `/bench/repo/internal/idp/oauth2/oauth2_test.go` (tests)\n\nThe shipped concrete protocol is **OAuth2**. File header: `// Package oauth2 implements the OAuth2 identity provider integration.` It provides:\n- `type IdentityProvider struct { config *storepb.OAuth2Config }`\n- `NewIdentityProvider(config *storepb.OAuth2Config)`\n- `ExchangeToken(...)` — OAuth2 code exchange, with PKCE support\n- `UserInfo(...)` — returns `*idp.IdentityProviderUserInfo` (linking back to the abstraction)\n\n### Confirmation it is the only protocol implementation\n\n- `internal/idp` contains exactly one subpackage: `oauth2`. No `oidc`, `saml`, or `ldap` packages exist.\n- The store proto enum confirms only OAuth2 is supported: `/bench/repo/proto/gen/store/idp.pb.go` defines `IdentityProvider_Type` with only `TYPE_UNSPECIFIED = 0` and `OAUTH2 = 1`. The config oneof (`IdentityProviderConfig`) has a single variant, `IdentityProviderConfig_Oauth2Config` wrapping `OAuth2Config`.\n\n### Wiring (how the two packages are used together)\n\n`/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/auth_service_sso.go` is the SSO login flow. In `resolveSSOIdentity` it branches on `identityProvider.Type == storepb.IdentityProvider_OAUTH2`, calls `oauth2.NewIdentityProvider(...)`, then `ExchangeToken` / `UserInfo`, and consumes the result as `*idp.IdentityProviderUserInfo`. Related handlers: `/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/idp_service.go` (IdP CRUD) and `/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/auth_service.go`.\n\n**Answer:** abstraction package = `internal/idp`; concrete protocol implementation package = `internal/idp/oauth2` (OAuth2, the only protocol that ships)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":23012,"output_tokens":1216,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":800},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CdkPjrjX34boptpj7BRGN","attributionAgent":"Explore","type":"assistant","uuid":"a235c9de-80ac-49c2-926f-1a46bdcfbe4b","timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:30:28.950Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/bench/repo","sessionId":"0dc1113e-88b9-418f-a888-bf0cbba51028","version":"2.1.221","git